  "notes": "Icy Veins could not be read: icy-veins.com/wow-classic/classic-engineering-profession-guide returns HTTP 403 to WebFetch and a Cloudflare bot check in the browser, so there are no Icy Veins alts. The Wowhead guide is patch 1.15.x. The guide's table has two overlapping rows, '135 - 145 Heavy Blasting Powder' then '135 - 150 Whirring Bronze Gizmo'; the second is recorded as 145-150 to keep the steps contiguous. Product item IDs are from the guide's links where it links the product (4357, 4359, 4364, 4371, 4375, 4377, 4382, 10498, 6219, 10505, 10560, 10561, 15992, 15997); the rest come from each Wowhead spell page's Create Item link. Reagent counts per craft are the guide's totals divided by its craft count. Thorium Tube reagents (6 Thorium Bar) come from its spell page, and the guide gives no craft count for it ('if you can't get this, do Thorium Tube instead'). made: null everywhere because WebFetch never shows the number made. The guide's numbers are crafts, so e.g. Thorium Shells and Coarse Dynamite make more than 1 per craft in game; read GetTradeSkillNumMade. learnAt is known only where the guide states it: Arclight Spanner 50 and Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor 175 ('Engineering trainers at skill N'), Hi-Explosive Bomb 235 and Dense Blasting Powder 250 (Buzzek Bracketswing list). The rest are null. Hi-Explosive Bomb and Dense Blasting Powder are taught by Buzzek Bracketswing in Gadgetzan, who is also the only Artisan trainer (225-300). Schematic: Thorium Widget is item 16042, sold by Sovik (Orgrimmar) / Gearcutter Cogspinner (Ironforge). Schematic: Thorium Shells is item 16051, a BoE world drop. Tools needed in bags: Blacksmith Hammer 5956, Arclight Spanner 6219, Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor 10498. Ranks: Journeyman 50-75 (char lvl 10), Expert 125-150 (lvl 20), Artisan 200-225 (lvl 35). Specialisations, not in steps: Gnomish or Goblin Engineering at skill 200 and char level 30, via quest; Goblin Engineer spell 20222. Gnome racial Engineering Specialization (spell 20593) gives +15."
